1
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:22,620
October 14th, 2012 — millions of viewers watch 
as skydiver Felix Baumgartner ascends to the  

2
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:27,480
edge of space, takes a small step, and then 
free falls about 120,000 feet down to Earth.  

3
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:32,400
During his descent, he not only broke the sound 
barrier but a handful of world records as well.

4
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:37,380
However, this spectacle was not from NASA 
or Space X… When you look a little closer,  

5
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:40,260
you see the unmistakable symbol of Red Bull.

6
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:45,000
Of course, this is just one of countless 
examples of Red Bull’s extreme and unorthodox  

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,800
marketing strategies - they’re responsible 
for 10 story motorcycle jumps, snowboarding  

8
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:54,540
down an active volcano, not to mention owning 
multiple racing, football and e-sports teams.

9
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:58,980
So how did this simple energy drink, 
which started out as an obscure,  

10
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:02,040
medicinal syrup, become not only 
one of the biggest disruptors in  

11
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:05,160
the beverage industry but also one 
of the best-marketed products ever?

12
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:10,380
By the end of 2022, the Global Energy Drink 
industry will be worth around $90 billion dollars,  

13
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:15,960
and sitting on top of the caffeinated throne 
is Red Bull, who in 2021 alone sold more than  

14
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:21,420
9.8 billion cans across 172 countries — more 
than one can for every person on the planet!

15
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:26,520
And yet despite this, Red Bull began from 
the most unlikely and humble of beginnings.

16
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:34,860
Chaleo Yoovidhya  

17
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:41,400
was born in rural Thailand, and his parents 
were duck farmers who also sold fruit. They  

18
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:44,460
had very little money, and couldn’t 
afford to give their children a formal  

19
00:01:44,460 --> 00:01:49,140
education. Thus Chaleo grew up working 
on a farm, with very little prospects.

20
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:52,680
However when his parents sent him off to 
Bangkok to go and work with his brother as  

21
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:57,480
a pharmaceutical sales rep, he worked extremely 
hard, and saved up enough money that in 1956,  

22
00:01:57,480 --> 00:02:01,920
he was able to open his own small business 
which he called T.C. Pharmaceutical Industries.  

23
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:07,260
Initially the business was designed purely to 
sell medicines, such as antibiotics he imported.

24
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:11,760
However, around this time, pharmaceutical 
companies in Japan had started creating  

25
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:15,240
herbal syrups labeled “energizing 
tonics.” They were a big hit,  

26
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:17,760
and soon started getting 
imported to Thailand as well.

27
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:21,180
After nearly ten years of running 
T.C. Pharmaceutical Industries,  

28
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:25,080
Chaleo decided he wanted to create his 
own version of these energy tonics.

29
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:29,880
However Chaleo saw that the current products 
on the market were quite expensive and targeted  

30
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:34,260
more towards wealthier consumers. Given that he 
came from poverty himself, he knew that it was  

31
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:39,120
actually the blue collar working man who needed 
energy much more. Construction workers, farmers,  

32
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:42,780
people doing lots of long physical labour 
which required constant attention and energy.

33
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:47,280
So after analyzing the formulas of other 
drinks on the market, Chaleo created his  

34
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:52,440
own similar elixir containing caffeine, B 
vitamins, and a chemical called taurine. But,  

35
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:56,820
what truly set Chaleo’s concoction apart from the 
competition was the inclusion of large amounts of  

36
00:02:56,820 --> 00:03:00,180
sugar, giving the syrup a more appealing 
flavor, and even more of an energy boost.

37
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:05,340
He named the beverage Krating Daeng. In 
Thai, Daeng means red, which, for him  

38
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:09,600
symbolized perseverance. But Krating doesn’t 
technically mean bull. It actually means gaur,  

39
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:14,220
which is a relative of the water buffalo, and the 
largest species of wild cattle in the world. The  

40
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:18,480
reason for the choice is that Chaleo wanted the 
brand rooted in imagery of strength and power.

41
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:22,260
However, his new drink was hardly 
an overnight success. At the time,  

42
00:03:22,260 --> 00:03:25,680
products from countries like Japan 
and South Korea dominated the market.  

43
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:29,940
But Chaleo’s decision to focus more on 
provincial and rural parts of Thailand,  

44
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:34,620
unlike his competitors who focused on big 
cities like Bangkok, proved to be a wise choice.

45
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:38,760
To get things started, Chaleo gave some 
free samples to truck drivers who were  

46
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:40,860
working long hours and needed help staying alert,  

47
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:45,660
and pitched it as a stimulant to improve 
energy and concentration. It then steadily  

48
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:49,860
grew via word of mouth and began to grow in 
popularity amongst Thailand’s working class.

49
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:54,180
Using the money from initial sales, 
Chaleo began sponsoring Muay Thai matches,  

50
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:57,960
which was the most popular martial art in 
Thailand, and a big part of Thai culture.  

51
00:03:57,960 --> 00:04:02,760
This not only helped his drink get recognition, 
but created an association with high energy and  

52
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:06,840
power. This was a great strategy, because 
most of the other energy drinks at the time  

53
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:10,920
were pretty generic, whereas right from the 
start Chaleo focused on building a brand,  

54
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:14,940
and his drink almost became a symbol of 
perseverance amongst the working class.

55
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:18,840
By 1980, his product had become 
a big success all over Thailand.

56
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:23,940
However, it was an unlikely encounter with 
an Austrian businessman selling toothpaste,  

57
00:04:23,940 --> 00:04:27,300
that would soon make this drink a 
multi-billion dollar global empire.

58
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:39,060
Whilst it was Chaleo who first created the 
drink that would later become known as Red Bull,  

59
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:42,840
it was a man named Dietrich Mateschitz who 
helped the business become what it is today.

60
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:48,120
Dietrich had studied World Trade at the University 
of Commerce in Vienna. Although between partying,  

61
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:52,440
traveling, and chasing girls, It took 
him 10 years to graduate. However he was  

62
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:56,700
always known for his wild imaginative 
ideas, and after graduating had worked  

63
00:04:56,700 --> 00:05:01,260
his way up to become international marketing 
director of a German company called Blendax,  

64
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:04,800
who manufactured products like skin 
creams, shampoo and toothpaste.

65
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:07,380
As part of his job Dietrich had to travel all over  

66
00:05:07,380 --> 00:05:11,160
the world. This meant many long days 
and nights of airports and flights.

67
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:15,900
On one particularly exhausting trip from Europe 
to Thailand, where he was meant to be attending  

68
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:20,220
an important meeting, he felt so tired that he 
went into a local store and asked if there was  

69
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:24,720
anything that could help him. It was here that he 
discovered Chaleo’s energy drink, Krating Daeng.

70
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:28,500
Dietrich tried it, and in just a few minutes 
he not only felt much more energized,  

71
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:31,620
he no longer had his jet lag. 
He became an avid drinker of  

72
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:34,800
the product - but at the time it 
was only available in Thailand.

73
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:38,820
Shortly after this, Dietrich read in a 
newspaper that the highest tax payer in Japan,  

74
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:42,780
was another one of these energy drinks. 
This confirmed to him just how popular  

75
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:46,140
these products were in Asia - and yet there 
was nothing really like it in the west.

76
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:50,160
Now to be honest, Dietrich had been getting 
kind of bored of his job at Blendax,  

77
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:54,180
and so he decided to make a very bold 
move. He quit his well paying job,  

78
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:58,800
and tracked down Chaleo, saying he wanted to go 
into business with him. Dietrich’s plan was to  

79
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:02,640
take Chaleo’s energy drink international 
and introduce it to European consumers.

80
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:05,640
After a little persuading, the two 
men went into business together,  

81
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:10,440
each putting in $500,000 dollars of their 
savings. They agreed Dietrich would run the  

82
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:13,620
operational side, whilst Chaleo would 
continue to focus on the product side.  

83
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:18,240
They both got 49% of the company, with 
the remaining 2% going to Chaleo’s son.

84
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:21,720
Dietrich’s first big decision was that they 
should form a new separate company for this  

85
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:25,980
called Red Bull, which would be simpler and more 
memorable than the literal translation of Red  

86
00:06:25,980 --> 00:06:31,440
Gaur. And thus, in 1984, Red Bull officially was 
founded in Dietrich’s home country of Austria.

87
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:36,660
However, before launching, they did some customer 
research to test how European audiences responded  

88
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:42,240
to the product… and the feedback was awful.
Trial groups said the drink tasted ‘disgusting’.  

89
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:46,380
Market research suggested the drink was 
too unhealthy and not appealing at all.

90
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:51,480
But the two Red Bull founders so strongly believed 
in the idea, that they pushed on anyway. They made  

91
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:55,560
some important changes using the feedback though 
- like carbonating the drink and switching to  

92
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:59,520
a slimmer sleek silver can which looked more 
premium, and distinguished it from competitors.

93
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:02,400
Dietrich also said that in order 
to feel like a premium product,  

94
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:06,420
they had to have a premium price - and so 
they charged nearly double what consumers  

95
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:10,320
were used to paying for other carbonated 
drinks. Pricing this high seemed like a  

96
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:13,740
very risky move, but would later prove 
to be crucial to the company’s success.

97
00:07:13,740 --> 00:07:18,600
They also decided on the now famous slogan “Red 
Bull gives you wings” to represent a product  

98
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:22,680
that provides energy, focus, and potential. 
This would later cause controversy though,  

99
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:27,120
but for now in 1987, Red Bull was 
finally ready to be released in the West.

