115
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:43,080
On April 1, 1987, Red Bull launched in Austria - 
and to create the premium feel Dietrich wanted,  

116
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:46,140
the beverage was initially offered 
at trendy Austrian ski resorts.

117
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:50,700
To begin with, Red Bull had a very small team 
of just a single secretary and a six-person  

118
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:55,500
sales force. And since they had an extremely small 
marketing budget, Dietrich knew he couldn’t afford  

119
00:08:55,500 --> 00:09:00,300
expensive TV ads or elaborate campaigns like 
other drink companies. Instead, he initially  

120
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:04,080
relied on more creative lower cost marketing 
strategies to spread the word about Red Bull.

121
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:07,800
Firstly, they reached out to popular, 
charismatic, and influential college  

122
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:11,520
students. They would then give them cases 
of Red Bull for free and have them drive  

123
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:16,200
around campus in Mini Coopers decorated with 
enormous Red Bull cans on top. They also gave  

124
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:20,160
these students money to throw parties where 
Red Bull was given out. The idea was that  

125
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:23,820
these popular students would shape the buying 
habits of their friends and fellow students.

126
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:27,060
In fact, they even started hiring 
attractive women to be “Red Bull  

127
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:29,940
Girls” and just hand out free 
drinks on university campuses.

128
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:34,320
Meanwhile, Red Bull salespeople, called 
“Musketeers,” offered free coolers to bars,  

129
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:36,900
inspiring bartenders to feature 
the beverage in new cocktails,  

130
00:09:37,620 --> 00:09:40,560
which helped Red Bull become known 
as a mixer with alcoholic drinks.

131
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:44,100
Red Bull even began leaving empty 
cans in bars and nightclubs,  

132
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:47,820
so that people would constantly see the logo 
and be curious to try the drink themselves.

133
00:09:47,820 --> 00:09:52,980
All these tactics proved successful, and Red 
Bull sold over 1 million cans in the first year.

134
00:09:52,980 --> 00:09:56,040
However, financially, they 
actually made a loss that year,  

135
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:59,160
since they’d given away so many free 
products as part of these marketing  

136
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:03,300
schemes. But Dietrich knew that investing in 
their brand, especially in the early stages,  

137
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:08,520
would pay dividends later. And he was right. By 
the second year, sales doubled to 2 million cans,  

138
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:13,560
and again to 4 million cans by the third year. Red 
Bull spread across Europe, and at one point got so  

139
00:10:13,560 --> 00:10:17,220
popular in Germany that they actually couldn’t 
produce enough cans to keep up with the demand.

140
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:21,720
Of course, despite the growth, competing 
in mainstream advertising like TV ads  

141
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:25,380
was still a very expensive option. But 
Dietrich had always loved extreme sports,  

142
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:29,760
and realized very few big companies seemed to 
be sponsoring these events, like for example  

143
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:34,680
cliff diving. Sponsoring extreme sports helped 
sell red bull as more than just an energy drink;  

144
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:39,720
but a lifestyle. Red bull became associated 
with daredevils and high adrenaline activities.

145
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:44,580
By 1997, Red Bull was ready for its 
US debut. Although by that point,  

146
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:49,620
the energy drink market had become a $1.7 billion 
business, and thus a lot more competition had  

147
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:54,540
entered the market. And unlike beverage rivals 
such as Coca-Cola, Red Bull has no secret,  

148
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:58,980
patented formula. All the ingredients are 
clearly labeled on the can. And initially  

149
00:10:58,980 --> 00:11:03,120
Red Bull literally just offered one flavor, 
which typically performed poorly in taste tests.

150
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:07,800
And yet despite this, Red Bull sales 
continued to rise. In an interview,  

151
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:12,420
Dietrich was asked why he didn’t try to make a 
better-tasting product. To which he replied that  

152
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:16,320
Red Bull was never about the product itself, 
but building a brand around an experience.

153
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:21,540
You see at its core, Red Bull never set out to 
be a beverage company. It was a story-telling  

154
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:25,620
company. The goal was to bring customers into 
that evolving myth, instead of trying to cram  

155
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:30,000
a product into their lives. To achieve this, 
the company has taken great efforts to attach  

156
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:34,080
itself to a growing collection of events, and 
spectacles that entice customers to the brand.

157
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:39,120
Red Bull spends far more than most companies on 
marketing - but instead of merely running ads  

158
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:43,380
on why you should buy the drink or sponsoring 
a single event, Red Bull will purchase entire  

159
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:47,640
sports teams, construct in-house media 
companies, and host world-class events.

160
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:52,020
It all began with Austrian Formula 1 legend 
Gerhard Berger who became Red Bull's first  

161
00:11:52,020 --> 00:11:56,880
sponsored athlete in 1989. But today, 
the company sponsors over 500 athletes,  

162
00:11:56,880 --> 00:12:00,060
daredevils, and adventurers, spanning 
the entire field of professional and  

163
00:12:00,060 --> 00:12:05,580
amateur sports — from football to Ice Hockey, 
Formula 1, and even E-Sports. Interestingly,  

164
00:12:05,580 --> 00:12:09,720
this has actually opened up other revenue streams 
for the company - for example they make money  

165
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:14,220
from formula 1 prizes and sponsorships, giving 
them yet more money to re-invest in marketing.

166
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:19,200
But this long-term approach is extremely 
effective, because for example, by owning  

167
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:23,100
a team like the New York red bulls, every 
time the media or fans are discussing the  

168
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:26,880
team it’s naturally bringing red bull into 
the conversation and people’s subconscious.

169
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:31,980
The company even invented its own sporting 
events. The Flugtag, created in 2000,  

170
00:12:31,980 --> 00:12:35,520
is the German word for “flying day.” 
During this event Red Bull created,  

171
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:39,780
hundreds of teams worldwide compete in 
homemade flying machines to see how far  

172
00:12:39,780 --> 00:12:44,460
their wild creations can fly. And if you’re 
wondering, the current record stands at 258  

173
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:48,780
feet. By creating events in which its product 
can be served and its brand narrative can unfold,  

174
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:53,820
Red Bull has again successfully turned expenses 
into a successful revenue stream all on its own.

175
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:57,900
Outside of the world of sports, Red Bull 
also sponsors art and music events such  

176
00:12:57,900 --> 00:13:02,700
as Lollapalooza and Austin City Limits. And 
of course, by 2012, the company was sending  

177
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:07,500
daredevils to the edge of space to jump out and 
free fall at over 800 miles per hour! And despite  

178
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:11,100
taking years to plan and tens of millions 
of dollars, it seems like it was worth it.  

179
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:15,420
The YouTube video of this set a world record for 
most concurrent live streams, and has gone on to  

180
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:20,580
reach well over 120 million views. After right 
this, the company saw global sales rise by 13%.

181
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:25,380
When Red Bull create these memorable events or 
set world records, they’re often talked about  

182
00:13:25,380 --> 00:13:30,120
or watched long after they happen, providing a 
great steady long-term return on their investment. 

183
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:33,900
But here’s the most interesting and 
unique part of Red Bull’s strategy:  

184
00:13:33,900 --> 00:13:39,420
during all these events and spectacles the company 
puts on, they hardly ever refer to their drink.

185
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:43,920
For example with Baumgartner's record breaking 
freefall, most companies would probably have made  

186
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:47,940
sure that when he landed he was seen drinking a 
can of red bull - but there was no mention of the  

187
00:13:47,940 --> 00:13:52,020
drink. And that’s because Red Bull’s advertising 
so often doesn’t feel like advertising.

188
00:13:52,020 --> 00:13:56,700
Red Bull aim for brand recognition rather than 
actively selling their product. They try to make  

189
00:13:56,700 --> 00:14:01,140
something exciting for their audience to simply 
associate their brand with incredible things.

190
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:05,160
And in a world where we are inundated 
with ads in our face and sales pitches,  

191
00:14:05,160 --> 00:14:09,240
this more subtle approach is effective. 
As then it doesn’t cheapen the spectacle.  

192
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:12,180
It doesn’t feel like we’re watching 
an ad, it feels more like we’re just  

193
00:14:12,180 --> 00:14:15,480
watching something cool from a company 
who happens to also sell energy drinks.

194
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:19,860
The truth is Red Bull isn’t really a drinks 
company, it’s really a marketing company. And  

195
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:23,460
as a result they’ve been able to position 
Red Bull as more of a premium lifestyle  

196
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:28,380
product - which ironically is the total opposite 
of how it began in Thailand for blue collar  

197
00:14:28,380 --> 00:14:32,760
workers. Red Bull started out as the cheapest 
energy drink, now it’s one of the most expensive.  

198
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:37,020
The recipe hasn’t really changed, that’s just 
the power of great marketing and branding.

199
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:41,160
As a result, in some countries today, Red 
Bull has more than 80% market share of  

200
00:14:41,160 --> 00:14:45,780
energy drinks. And since 1987, over 100 
Billion cans have been sold worldwide.

201
00:14:45,780 --> 00:14:50,340
However… you don’t become the number one 
energy drink without a little controversy…

202
00:14:56,580 --> 00:15:03,180
Red Bull has been banned in numerous countries 
over the years, most famously in France. When  

203
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:06,840
a teenager died after drinking multiple 
cans of Red Bull during a basketball match,  

204
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:11,040
there was understandably a lot of panic. Now, 
there was no evidence actually found that red  

205
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:15,240
bull caused the death, but it still prompted 
accusations that the drink’s caffeine content  

206
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:19,440
was excessive and that some of Red Bull’s other 
ingredients might not be as safe as they made out. 

207
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:23,280
However, by 2008, the full version of 
Red Bull was for sale in France again,  

208
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:27,120
since Red Bull successfully argued that there 
wasn’t sufficient evidence that any of the  

209
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:31,800
ingredients were harmful. I mean it wasn’t exactly 
healthy, but not unhealthy enough to be banned.

210
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:36,840
Then in Germany in 2009 red bull cola was 
found to contain trace amounts of cocaine,  

211
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:40,320
causing some German states to pull 
the drink as well. But once again,  

212
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:44,160
after further research it was found to be 
such a negligible amount that you’d have to  

213
00:15:44,160 --> 00:15:48,540
drink almost impossible amounts to actually feel 
anything, so the drink was reinstated there too.

214
00:15:48,540 --> 00:15:53,820
In 2013, Red Bull came under fire again when it 
was sued for false advertising over its slogan  

215
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:58,980
‘red bull gives you wings’. Now to be fair to 
red bull here, surely nobody actually expected  

216
00:15:58,980 --> 00:16:03,780
to grow literal wings and fly, so this lawsuit 
seemed like a frivolous cash grab. But they  

217
00:16:03,780 --> 00:16:07,260
managed to argue that since red bull didn’t 
give any functional athletic improvement,  

218
00:16:07,260 --> 00:16:11,880
it was false advertising - and Red bull ended up 
paying $13 million dollars to settle the lawsuit.

219
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:16,500
Now so far these issues all seem kinda 
harsh against Red Bull. But actually the  

220
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:20,280
real controversy about Red Bull is the one 
that most people in the west don’t even seem  

221
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:25,380
to know about. You see in 2012, the heir 
to red bull’s fortune, Chaleo’s grandson,  

222
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:29,040
was accused of running over a policeman 
and killing him while speeding in his  

223
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:33,600
Ferrari. It’s then reported he didn’t attend 
court, and instead fled the country. Despite  

224
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:37,800
there being seemingly overwhelming evidence 
against him, the case has not been perused,  

225
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:42,720
and in Thailand its seen as an egregious example 
of how the ultra wealthy and powerful are above  

226
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:47,340
the law and can get away with anything. This 
prompted headlines like: Red Bull Heir Shows How  

227
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:52,200
to Get Away With Killing a Cop in Thailand, with 
some even starting a campaign to boycott Red Bull.

228
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:55,500
Now to be fair, it’s not like 
the heir to Red Bull’s fortune  

229
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:58,380
is actually involved in running 
the company, but it’s certainly  

230
00:16:58,380 --> 00:17:02,220
a strain on the perfect image that Red 
Bull spends so much money to maintain.

231
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:06,300
However, Red Bull’s original creator 
Chaleo would not be around to see that,  

232
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:11,940
as he died just a few months before the incident 
in March 2012, aged 88. When he passed away he  

233
00:17:11,940 --> 00:17:16,440
was Thailand’s third richest person with an 
estimated $5 billion dollar fortune. And in  

234
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:20,760
fact, still to this day, his co-founder Dietrich 
is the richest person in Austria. That’s because  

235
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:24,480
Red Bull is still a private company; the 
founders never had to sell loads of their  

236
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:28,200
equity as they had such great profit margins 
and could keep reinvesting back into the  

237
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:32,460
business using the profits they made. So they 
both became obscenely wealthy. And actually,  

238
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:35,520
I think there’s several lessons all of 
us should be learning from Red Bull…

239
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:48,360
Firstly, Red Bull is proof that sometimes you 
don’t need to invent something totally new,  

240
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:50,880
you can bring an existing product to a new market  

241
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:54,120
or audience and have massive success 
by just putting your own spin on it.

242
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:58,620
Secondly, it’s clearly a very effective strategy 
to find a product that’s cheap to manufacture,  

243
00:17:58,620 --> 00:18:03,060
and then invest heavily in marketing to create a 
more premium feel and brand image for the product,  

244
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:06,480
so you can charge higher prices. 
That’ll give you high profit margins,  

245
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:09,360
giving you huge amounts of money 
to invest in even more marketing,  

246
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:13,500
and thus create a virtuous cycle of growth. 
For context, some sources have estimated  

247
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:18,000
Red Bull costs about 9 cents per can to 
make, yet sell them for $1.79 or more.

248
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:22,380
And finally, Red Bull is a reminder that 
the best marketing is not just running ads  

249
00:18:22,380 --> 00:18:26,580
the exact same way everyone does, it’s actually 
doing something creative and original - because  

250
00:18:26,580 --> 00:18:31,620
the ultimate lesson from Red Bull is to not just 
sell a product, but sell a feeling. Sell an image.

251
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:35,520
And, there is perhaps just one company that 
has done an even better job of this than Red  

252
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:39,360
Bull. If you wanna learn the dark secrets 
of how Coca-Cola make billions of dollars  

253
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:43,140
despite all of the controversies they’ve been 
involved with, check out the disturbing history  

254
00:18:43,140 --> 00:18:48,720
of Coca-Cola by clicking right here. Trust me, 
it’s a crazy one. I’ll see you there. Cheers.

